You have Adie\'92s tonic pupil. This means that one of your pupils reacts more slowly to light and may stay slightly larger than the other. This happens because of a change in the nerve supply to the pupil. It is usually a benign condition and often occurs without a serious underlying cause.\
\
It is common to notice light sensitivity, difficulty focusing at near, or a difference in pupil size. In many cases, the condition stabilizes over time and does not progress.\
